{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ce5d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a079e0-55db-79f2-85b0-c8c2e4c1a43f"},"sequence":1417,"recorded_at":1780531400002829,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3e1277eb-45fc-4f67-a96e-3b0bc6460b15"},"task_id":"3e1277eb-45fc-4f67-a96e-3b0bc6460b15","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3e1277eb-45fc-4f67-a96e-3b0bc6460b15","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 50-66\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-//   - Digit spellings outside the classifier, completed per review\n-//     N-R1 (three semantically identical spellings measured green at\n-//     9/9 with no such site in either package, reviewer-grepped):\n-//     1. integer code points (`c < 0x30`, `c > 57`) are ENUMERATED:\n-//     digitGuardDigitRune admits token.INT 48..57 in every base,\n-//     pinned by TestDigitGuardDigitRuneAdmitsCodePointSpellings;\n-//     2. named rune constants (`const zero = '0'; c < zero`) are\n-//     OUTSIDE: an identifier is not a literal, so the comparison\n-//     classifies as other and the chain prunes. No such site\n-//     exists in either package today;\n-//     3. strconv-delegated admission (`strconv.Atoi` + error branch)\n-//     is OUTSIDE: it is not a comparison at all, so there is no\n-//     chain to classify. No such site exists in either package\n-//     today. A new site in either spelling must widen the\n-//     classifier (named constants) or the census shape\n-//     (delegation) instead of passing silently; the census still\n-//     fails closed on every comparison it CAN see.\n+//   - Digit spellings outside the comparison classifier, completed per\n+//     review N-R1 (three semantically identical spellings; the earlier\n+//     \"no such site in either package\" claim was false for the third\n+//     and is corrected here, not repeated):\n+//     1. integer code points (`c < 0x30`, `c > 57`) are ENUMERATED:\n+//     digitGuardDigitRune admits token.INT 48..57 in every base,\n+//     pinned by TestDigitGuardDigitRuneAdmitsCodePointSpellings;\n+//     2. named rune constants (`const zero = '0'; c < zero`) are\n+//     OUTSIDE: an identifier is not a literal, so the comparison\n+//     classifies as other and the chain prunes. No such site\n+//     exists in either package today (reviewer-grepped at N-R1,\n+//     re-verified here by the census passing with the classifier\n+//     unchanged: a named-constant gate would classify as other and\n+//     fail as unclassifiable, not pass silently);\n+//     3. strconv-delegated admission is OUTSIDE the comparison\n+//     classifier: it is not a comparison at all, so there is no\n+//     chain to classify. One such site EXISTS:\n+//     internal/provhost/opdecode.go rawUint53\n+//     (`strconv.ParseUint(literal, 10, 64)` + error branch +\n+//     magnitude bound `parsed > maxUint53`). It is behaviorally\n+//     pinned, not censused: narrowing the bound to `maxUint53+1`\n+//     (admitting exactly 2^53) reddens\n+//     TestDecodeQuiesceRefusals/count_overflow, which admits the\n+//     maximal uint53 and refuses 2^53. A second delegated site is\n+//     covered only if it carries the same shape of behavioral pin;\n+//     the census still fails closed on every comparison it CAN see.\n"}}}
