{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000da51","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a079e0-55db-79f2-85b0-c8c2e4c1a43f"},"sequence":2947,"recorded_at":1780531400005889,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"8581ca2f-ce28-495a-8b78-d3072f738fae"},"task_id":"8581ca2f-ce28-495a-8b78-d3072f738fae","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"8581ca2f-ce28-495a-8b78-d3072f738fae","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-97-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-07\\n\\n### 0648 — v8heil: inventory machinery unified on invcore, tb ported to executed witnesses\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-v8heil. No production change (12 modified paths all `*_test.go`). New `internal/invcore` (ScanProduction/MustScanProduction, ParseBytes, DiffSets, ConstructorSpec+MustAuditConstructorReferences+WatchedCallPositions, SiteRecorder) + `terminalbackend/refusal_arm_witnesses_test.go` (184/210 arms executed at entry, 26 stated-bound rows pinned) + `TestQualifiedWatchesAdmitsPrefixSpellings` pin.\\n- FINDING (measured): provider records refusals at construction, so swallowing a built refusal downstream is census-invisible — D-pv mutant killed by the witness only, audit green. Execution-recorded, not outcome-recorded.\\n- FINDING: the `Errorf*` prefix stem had no pin (exact-`Errorf` plants passed without it); unit pin added, N-core-errorf-prefix kills through it.\\n- FINDING (harness): scoped `-run` silently skips provider's TestMain audit and early masks ran 0 tests in the wrong package — runner records ran-counts per mask and supports full-package census masks.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-v8heil_outcome.md` + `battery_v8heil.json` (15 applied/15 killed/0 survived + control rows; 9 census-only, 1 behav-only, 2 both, 3 provider-audit) attached as task resources. Census: tb 210=210, ph 167/15=167/15, pv 6/18/0/0=6/18/0/0. AC ratio 369/395 driven + 26 stated-bound. Candidate tree verified by `ls-tree` + `hash-object` (OID in the outcome doc).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (23 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-race` exit 0 (23 ok), `-cover` exit 0 (invcore 71.0%, provhost 86.0%, provider 97.8%, terminalbackend 94.9%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok, catalog current, cigate contracts pass.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n## 2026-09-06\\n\\n### 2255 — review round 6: listing census replaced by one derived enumeration over both digit-guard shapes (F1/F2)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (fourth consecutive round of the digit-edge class). No production change. Deleted `terminalbackend/digit_range_census_test.go` (listed its own sites, scoped out the accumulation bounds); new `terminalbackend/digit_guard_census_test.go` derives 9 sites in one AST pass over terminalbackend+provhost production — char (ordering vs a digit rune, incl. hex digit cases) and bound (ordering vs a same-function `*10` accumulator) — keyed structurally (rune values, accumulation steps, printer-normalized chains), with per-site rows (rejected class / threshold+witness) and three fail-closed arms (unregistered, orphan, unclassifiable). F1 witness: the 37-digit `9223372036854775808000000000000000001` on both geometry members (fails under the `> 922337203685477580` edge mutant, green at 100/1000/1e9/92233720368547758).\\n- FINDING (battery corrected the work, in-session): the first battery run left the hex token-preserving inserts (manifest `case digit == ':'`, surrogate `b == ':'`) SURVIVED with the condition edits census-only — the canonical-JSON sweeps never probe `:` inside an escape. New `TestDocumentHexEscapeDigitBoundaryRefused` / `TestProductionEntriesRefuseHexDigitBoundaryEscapes` drive `\\\\ud80:`/`\\\\udc0:` (malformed→syntax arm on real code, completing 0xD80A/0xDC0A lone surrogates under the mutant); both inserts are now BEHAVIORAL-ONLY kills with census exit 0. Lower edge (`/`) converts to 0xFFFF no surrogate prefix survives: widened lower bounds are verdict-equivalent on every input, measured by R6-D32/R6-D33 (behavioural green, census red) — a stated bound with a measurement, not prose.\\n- FINDING: the census keys survive renaming by construction — control plants prove it: a var-bound gate fails as `…|plantVarBindingTmp|char|octet < '0' || octet > '9'`, an import-aliased file as an unregistered site, plus plain/orphan/`== '5'`/bound plants; all six redden only the census test and revert SHA-256-clean.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round6.md` on the board task (9-site table, 33-row mutant table with per-arm split, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); harness `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_mut-round6.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_battery-round6.json` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_plants-round6.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_plants-round6.json` attached as task resources.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 86.0%, terminalbackend 94.3%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 36 sections, 98 cases), `GOOS=windows go build/vet` exit 0, `-race` exit 0 on provhost + terminalbackend. Battery: 33 applied / 33 killed / 0 survivors (narrowing 16/16, token-preserving 8/8 all behavioural-only, arm-deletion 9/9) + census-only C01 + NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL as distinct rows; masks calibrated non-empty (census 2 RUN, behavioural 460/671 RUN, all green pristine).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2254 — review round 5: saturation edge carried to semverMajor, geometry upper window closed, three-site digit census recorded (F1/F2)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (third consecutive round of the digit-edge class; the two new sites are both inside this leaf's delta in `internal/terminalbackend`). No production change: the `semverMajor` guard and the `descriptorGeometry` gate were already correct. Tests: new `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge` (largest exact fit 9223372036854775807, +1, aliasing witness 922337203685477580801.0.0 ±1, each requiring semverMajor==MaxInt AND refusal at ParseProviderDescriptor/CheckVersionTuple with the named arm, plus the witness at New); `1E2` rows on columns and rows in the value-refusals table; new `digit_range_census_test.go` recording all three leaf digit-range comparisons with per-site reachable rejected classes and declared equivalents, plus `TestDescriptorGeometryAdjacentsNeverReachTheGate` (`/`/`:` die at document syntax before the gate).\\n- FINDING (measured): weakened guard `major > math.MaxInt/10` admits 922337203685477580801.0.0 at ParseProviderDescriptor with err=nil (semverMajor returns 1, aliasing native major 1); weakened bound `digit > 'E'` admits `columns: 1E2` as Columns=312; both survived the whole 457-test suite. The neighbours refuse either way, so the value pins (==MaxInt) carry those kills — the round-4 lesson, re-applied. `+` is a declared equivalent (only legal after e/E, which refuses first); `/` and `:` are provably unreachable through json.Number.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round5.md` on the board task (F1/F2 tables, 9-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); harness `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_mut-round5.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_battery-round5.json` attached as task resources.\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 36 sections, 98 cases), `GOOS=windows go build/vet` exit 0, `-race` exit 0 on provhost + terminalbackend. Battery: 9 applied / 8 killed / 1 survived (T-D3 `+`, declared equivalent) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; the token-preserving narrowings (T-D1 killed, T-D3 equivalent, re-pinned P-M17 killed) all show zero census kill, and the arm-deletion T-D4 co-fires the census pair by construction.\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\\n\\n### 2253 — review round 4: parse-gate edges pinned behaviourally, census-only kills closed (F1a/F1b)\\n\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (F1a saturation-edge + F1b digit-range token-preserving, N4 peek-widening, N6 test-bound placement). No production change: `provhost/protocol.go` guard was already correct. Tests: new `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` (MaxInt, MaxInt+1, aliasing witness 922337203685477580802.0.0 ±1, each requiring parseMajor==MaxInt AND DecodeResponse incompatible_protocol/exit 6), new `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` ('/' 0x2F and ':' 0x3A in major and in each rest position, each requiring parseMajor unrecognized AND DecodeResponse provider_protocol_error/exit 13), new `TestDecodeResponseUnrecognizedVersionRunsMemberRules` (bare-frame member `ok` pins the peek widening). Doc: N2 CallExpr-only bound moved onto `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding` (N6).\\n- FINDING (measured): weakened guard `major > math.MaxInt/10` wraps 922337203685477580802.0.0 to major 2 (exit 13, aliasing native 2) while shipped saturates to MaxInt (exit 6); token-preserving inserts (`if digit == ':' { continue }`, `if rest[i] == '/' { continue }`, plus the '/' -in-major and ':'-in-rest mirrors) leave the derived arm set byte-identical (bijection 167/167) and survived the whole suite; peek widening `recognized || ...` slides bare-frame member `ok` to `protocol_version` with code/exit unchanged. All now redden behaviourally.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round4.md` on the board task (F1a/F1b tables, 22-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); battery script `mut_round4.py` + `battery-round4-all.json` under repo-root `.temp/TASK-260906-vmzk0y/`.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9516,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2379,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
