{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000da75","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a079e0-55db-79f2-85b0-c8c2e4c1a43f"},"sequence":2965,"recorded_at":1780531400005925,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"38173c32-e836-4324-8339-ee117e4249f1"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"06eb57d6-eaf6-4965-b2c6-a580e3455b69"},"task_id":"06eb57d6-eaf6-4965-b2c6-a580e3455b69","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"06eb57d6-eaf6-4965-b2c6-a580e3455b69","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-07\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-07\n+\n+### 0715 — v8heil round 2: site-recording seam closes the sibling-swallow class (F1/F2), all six findings fixed\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260906-v8heil rework (review rev2 CHANGES REQUESTED). Production seam in 4 files: `recordRefusal` hook (nil in prod) + `refuse` funnel (`//go:noinline`), hook calls in `mismatchf`/`integrityFailure`, 89 `&Error{}` literals routed through `refuse` same-line. Tests: new `refusal_site_audit_test.go` (TestMain exercised-line audit, row↔line mapping, skip pin, refuse-alias pins), line-carrying derivation with refuse-wrap enforcement, derived shadow-cover analysis replacing the 19 hand pairs, corrected N-R1 bound, dead loop deleted.\n+- FINDING (measured): pair-proves do not attribute — P8 plant left derivation identical + all 184 witnesses green; the audit kills it naming `conformance.go:713, :716`. The audit also caught a REAL pre-existing swallow on first run (`descriptor.go:123` never fired; #2 witness proved via sibling #1) — fixed as a witness (rename-away), not a bound.\n+- FINDING: clause sharing recomputed identically (62/184, 20 clauses, largest x11); death residual now 0/184. Stated remainder: rows bind to lines, witnesses do not (complementary swap invisible; shared with provider/provhost by construction).\n+- FINDING: F3's \"no strconv site\" was false — `provhost/opdecode.go rawUint53` exists, pinned by `count_overflow` (battery row B- reproduces the narrow-to-maxUint53+1 plant/kill).\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-v8heil_outcome-r2.md` + batteries (`battery_tb_r2` 8/8 incl. audit-only S-tb-shadow, `battery_ph_strconv` B-, re-ran core/pv/ph/x green; 19 applied/19 killed/0 survived + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct) attached as task resources. Census: tb 210/210 lines (26 bound, 14 codes), ph 167/15, pv 18/3. AC 4/4 rows, refusals 369/395 driven + 26 bound. Candidate tree `9d7eaa4d…` verified by `ls-tree` + `hash-object` (11/11 MATCH).\n+- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race` exit 0 (23 ok), `-cover` exit 0 (70.2/86.0/97.8/95.0), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok, catalog current, cigate pass.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n"}}}
